      "name": "Queue transparency: status updates and progress state for all waiting applicants",
      "kind": "ux_change",
      "description": "Extend proactive status messaging and in-journey progress indication to everyone in the manual review queue, not only applicants with a mobile number on file.",
      "horizon": "core",
      "supporting": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-57e6a3c3", "quote": "No idea whether anyone was looking at it. A progress bar would have been enough."},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-9cefd02f", "quote": "Six days and no update. I opened an account elsewhere in ten minutes."}
      ],
      "opposing": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-5a15ea40", "quote": "Abandonment among messaged applicants was 64% against 68% among applicants in the same period who were not messaged. Assignment was not random: messages were sent only to applicants who had supplied a mobile number."}
      ],
      "assessments": [
        {
          "dimension": "customer_reach",
          "state": "assessed",
          "summary": "Addressable population is the 5,489 applicants who abandoned in the queue in 2026-06, minus those unreachable; reachability is unquantified because mobile-number coverage is not in the pack (M9).",
          "citations": [
            {"evidence_id": "EV-19b9da2b", "quote": "value: 5489", "locator": "abandoned_in_manual_review_queue, 2026-06"}
          ],
          "support_level": "moderate"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "evidence_confidence",
          "state": "assessed",
          "summary": "Weak. The January 2026 result (64% vs 68%) was non-randomised and confounded by mobile-number possession, which plausibly correlates with completion regardless of messaging. The four-point gap cannot be read as an effect.",
          "citations": [
            {"evidence_id": "EV-5a15ea40", "quote": "Abandonment among messaged applicants was 64% against 68% among applicants in the same period who were not messaged. Assignment was not random: messages were sent only to applicants who had supplied a mobile number."}
          ],
          "support_level": "low"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "strategic_alignment",
          "state": "assessed",
          "summary": "Improves the wait experience but does not shorten it: routed applications still average 92.6 hours and p90 is 104 hours, against a 'minutes not days' ambition.",
          "citations": [
            {"evidence_id": "EV-587e5c4e", "quote": "value: 92.6", "locator": "mean_time_to_verify_hours, routed_to_manual_review"},
            {"evidence_id": "EV-99e35121", "quote": "value: 104", "locator": "p90_time_to_verify_hours, all"}
          ],
          "support_level": "moderate"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "risk",
          "state": "assessed",
          "summary": "Low regulatory exposure — no model, no biometric, no change to declines — but messaging that repeats requests for documents already supplied appears in feedback as an aggravating factor rather than a mitigation.",
          "citations": [
            {"evidence_id": "EV-da672a33", "quote": "Four days waiting and then a text asking for the same document again."}
          ],
          "support_level": "low"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "spend",
          "state": "cannot_assess",
          "summary": "No messaging cost or engineering estimate in the evidence.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "dimension": "financial_impact",
          "state": "cannot_assess",
          "summary": "No account value figure, and the messaging effect size is not credibly estimated.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "dimension": "delivery_effort",
          "state": "cannot_assess",
          "summary": "A messaging path already existed in January 2026, but no estimate for extending it to non-mobile channels is recorded.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "dimension": "product_usage",
          "state": "assessed",
          "summary": "Feedback repeatedly cites silence rather than duration as the trigger for giving up, including one respondent who converted quickly once a human engaged.",
          "citations": [
            {"evidence_id": "EV-9cefd02f", "quote": "Six days and no update. I opened an account elsewhere in ten minutes."},
            {"evidence_id": "EV-089c665f", "quote": "Speed of onboarding is the stated FY27 differentiator. Leadership has asked for a \"minutes not days\" experience."}
          ],
          "support_level": "low"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "strategic_customer_importance",
          "state": "cannot_assess",
          "summary": "No breakdown of queue-stage abandonment by age band or channel exists (M5, M8).",
          "citations": []
        }
      ],
      "why_not_selected": "Cheap and low-risk, but the only evidence for it is a confounded non-randomised comparison, and it manages the wait rather than removing it. Reasonable to bundle as a low-cost B-arm, not as the priority."
    },
    {
      "id": "A5",
      "name": "Instant Decision: automated approve/decline on the Veriphex score",
      "kind": "ai_automated",
      "description": "Use the Veriphex risk score to issue automated decisions within seconds, as proposed by the VP Growth for before the holiday season.",
      "horizon": "adjacent",
      "supporting": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-9b8dc246", "quote": "Instant Decision is the whole answer. Take the Veriphex score, approve or decline in ten seconds, done. I want it live before the holiday season."},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-60b0dd24", "quote": "value: 0.1", "locator": "mean_time_to_verify_hours, auto_decisioned — the speed prize if routing volume fell"}
      ],
      "opposing": [
        {"evidence_id": "EV-9cc6778c", "quote": "No application may be declined solely by an automated process. A named human reviewer must record their own decision and the basis for it before any decline is issued. This requirement has no confidence threshold and no volume exemption."},
        {"evidence_id": "EV-9b1eb068", "quote": "The Veriphex risk score is returned as a single integer between 0 and 999. No contributing factors, reason codes, or feature attributions are returned with it. Veriphex has confirmed in writing that the model internals are proprietary and will not be exposed to customers of the service."}
      ],
      "assessments": [
        {
          "dimension": "risk",
          "state": "assessed",
          "summary": "Highest risk option and partly impermissible as described. Declines may not be automated; declines need specific principal reasons the score cannot supply; and any model in the decision path must be inventoried with validation evidence by 2026-10-17 or be out of the path on the 2026-11-16 review date. The proposal to run legal review in parallel conflicts with the objectives document's own precedence rule.",
          "citations": [
            {"evidence_id": "EV-9cc6778c", "quote": "\"The automated system declined it\" is not a specific principal reason. An outcome the organisation cannot explain in specific terms is an outcome it may not issue."},
            {"evidence_id": "EV-9cc6778c", "quote": "A model not in the inventory by that date may not be in the decision path on the review date."},
            {"evidence_id": "EV-089c665f", "quote": "The remediation programme agreed with the supervisor in March 2026 takes precedence over growth work wherever the two conflict."}
          ],
          "support_level": "strong"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "evidence_confidence",
          "state": "assessed",
          "summary": "Lowest of all options. The only quantitative claim is a vendor figure with no baseline, population or comparison rules, and no back-test against this applicant population has ever been run.",
          "citations": [
            {"evidence_id": "EV-9b8dc246", "quote": "The pack does not state the baseline, the population, the routing rules it was compared against, or the market the figure came from. No independent evaluation was provided."},
            {"evidence_id": "EV-5a15ea40", "quote": "No experiment has tested automated decisioning of any kind, and no back-test of the Veriphex score against this applicant population has been run."}
          ],
          "support_level": "low"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "spend",
          "state": "assessed",
          "summary": "Blocked in the near term: no incremental vendor spend is approved before 2026-09-15, and any new vendor processing identity data needs a nine-to-eleven-week assessment before production traffic.",
          "citations": [
            {"evidence_id": "EV-089c665f", "quote": "No incremental vendor spend is approved before the Q3 planning review on 2026-09-15."},
            {"evidence_id": "EV-9cc6778c", "quote": "Any new vendor that processes applicant identity data requires a completed data protection assessment before it receives production traffic. Assessments currently take nine to eleven weeks."}
          ],
          "support_level": "strong"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "delivery_effort",
          "state": "assessed",
          "summary": "The date arithmetic does not work for a holiday launch: vendor assessment nine to eleven weeks, inventory and validation evidence by 2026-10-17, and a core banking freeze from 2026-10-01 to 2027-01-15.",
          "citations": [
            {"evidence_id": "EV-9cc6778c", "quote": "Every model that contributes to an account-opening decision must be entered in the model inventory, with completed validation evidence, no later than 30 days before that review — that is, by 2026-10-17."},
            {"evidence_id": "EV-9b1eb068", "quote": "A change freeze applies to the core banking platform from 2026-10-01 to 2027-01-15. Nothing that writes to account records ships inside that window."}
          ],
          "support_level": "strong"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "customer_reach",
          "state": "assessed",
          "summary": "In principle up to the 8,070 routed applications a month, but the share the score could clear is entirely unquantified for this population; the 62% vendor claim cannot be used as a reach estimate.",
          "citations": [
            {"evidence_id": "EV-28ab84eb", "quote": "value: 8070", "locator": "routed_to_manual_review, 2026-06"},
            {"evidence_id": "EV-9b8dc246", "quote": "A Veriphex briefing pack circulated before the meeting states that their score reduces manual review volume by 62%."}
          ],
          "support_level": "low"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "strategic_alignment",
          "state": "assessed",
          "summary": "Aligned with the speed differentiator in ambition, misaligned in sequencing: the remediation programme and the fixed 2026-11-16 review outrank growth work where they conflict.",
          "citations": [
            {"evidence_id": "EV-089c665f", "quote": "Speed of onboarding is the stated FY27 differentiator. Leadership has asked for a \"minutes not days\" experience."},
            {"evidence_id": "EV-9cc6778c", "quote": "Under the remediation letter of 2026-03-09 the organisation committed to an external model-risk review on 2026-11-16. The date is fixed and has been notified to the supervisor."}
          ],
          "support_level": "moderate"
        },
        {
          "dimension": "financial_impact",
          "state": "cannot_assess",
          "summary": "No licence cost, no cost per review avoided, no account value. Nothing in the pack allows a return estimate.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "dimension": "product_usage",
          "state": "cannot_assess",
          "summary": "The score is not currently in any decision path in the evidence, and no usage or coverage data is given.",
          "citations": []
        },
        {
          "dimension": "strategic_customer_importance",
          "state": "cannot_assess",
          "summary": "Untested for thin-file applicants, who are 47.8% of 18-24 routes; a bureau-derived score's behaviour on that segment is unknown without a back-test.",
          "citations": []
        }
      ],
      "why_not_selected": "As specified (automated decline in ten seconds) it conflicts directly with binding obligations, it has no in-population evidence, and no plausible path to being validated and inventoried before 2026-10-17. An approve-only variant with human declines is worth back-testing after the November review — but that is A8, not a build now."
